`mkDOS` generates an edge-refined asymmetric table and normalizes its represented
Steffen interpolant. Run `mkparameps` next to derive the matching normalized
first moment in `param.eps`. The continuum centroid is `0.175`; the checked-in
value includes only the roundoff of the represented table. This example does
not provide a transport function, so a matching `PHI.dat` is required before
running transport postprocessing.

For this choice of DOS, `<n> ~ 0.8` for `DOS.dat`.

`mkparameps-bubble` uses Bubble 1.14 with explicit Steffen interpolation,
visible quadrature warnings, best-effort finite results, and atomic output
publication to evaluate the first moment
`int(epsilon DOS(epsilon),-inf,inf)` in `param.eps-bubble`.
